# universal-argument bound to a single key (so it is recognised while an
# argument is being read), digit arguments in callback mode, EOF while
# reading an argument.  (universal-argument in callback mode crashes the 8.3
# reference in redisplay and is not tested.)
tags: emacs numarg
--- inputrc
"\C-o": universal-argument
--- script
readline "> "

=== universal-argument-key-twice
tags: universal-argument
keys: \C-o\C-ox<dump>\r

=== universal-argument-digits-then-key-terminates
tags: universal-argument
keys: \C-o3\C-ox<dump>\r

=== universal-argument-digits-then-key-then-command
tags: universal-argument
keys: abcdef\C-o2\C-o\C-b<dump>\r

=== universal-argument-eof-after-digits
tags: universal-argument eof
keys: abc\C-o2\C-o

=== digit-argument-eof
tags: digit-argument eof
keys: abc\M-2

=== callback-digit-argument
tags: digit-argument callback
--- script
callback "> "
--- keys
\M-1\M-2x<dump>\r

=== callback-digit-argument-then-meta-command
tags: digit-argument callback
--- script
callback "> "
--- keys
one two three\M-2\M-b<dump>\r
